From 7da184a4066b2f46b87f23f1083f4ac1e87f0ded Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 09:50:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] robo: range-based Production Date / Thickness edit +
 reordered Entry layout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Correct a whole run's Production Date or Thickness from the slab where it
changes, instead of editing every slab by hand.

- Edit slab gains an "apply to this slab and all following in the batch, up to
  the next change" toggle for Production Date and for Thickness. On save the
  value forward-fills within the batch (by S.No.) while slabs share the edited
  slab's OLD value, stopping at the first that already differs; earlier slabs are
  never touched. Works for a historical batch saved with one date/thickness on
  the whole run (a midnight crossing, or a mid-batch thickness change) and for
  new production. See src/lib/robo/rangeUpdate.ts (forwardRunIds) + the PATCH
  handler, scoped by batchRecipeId.
- Thickness becomes per-slab: display reads the slab's own thickness, else the
  batch setup's (roboThicknessOf) — Complete Details and the Production and Delay
  export sheets. Every existing row is NULL there and reads the setup exactly as
  before, so nothing already saved changes. New production still enters one
  thickness on the batch setup.
- An edit writes a per-slab Date/Thickness override ONLY when the operator
  actually changed it (or ticked apply-forward); an untouched field is left off
  the request, so it keeps falling back to the batch rather than being pinned.
- Robo Entry slab layout reordered and made responsive: Production Date leads,
  then S.No./Slab, In/Out, the Robo2 pair, and Remarks; two-up on tablet and
  desktop, stacked on a phone. The cross-midnight carry-forward is preserved.

No schema change — productionDate and thickness columns already exist. Verified:
tsc clean, 644 unit tests (incl. roboRangeUpdate/roboThickness), next build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
