From b4ef6d434a4a52df091f28bc6c7aef233f742b83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 06:13:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] robo(delays): fully editable delay log + multiple Robos
 per delay

Two changes to the slab Edit delay log.

EDITABLE. Existing delays were read-only; now every delay -- existing or newly
added -- is one editable row: change its code, machine(s), Start/End times or
remark independently, or remove it with the X. The save reconciles the whole
set: a delay with a DB id is updated in place, one without is created, and any
existing delay dropped from the list is deleted -- edit + remove + add in one
pass, with no duplicates, and a slab can be saved with no delays at all. The
existing "+ Add" form (searchable code picker, add-new-code) is unchanged. Only
the delay handling in the production PATCH changed, from append-only to a
reconcile that runs only when `delays` is present in the request.

MULTIPLE ROBOS. The machine field is now multi-select over the same four Robos:
one delay can name Robo2 + Robo3 and stays ONE record. No schema change -- the
names live comma-joined in the existing machineName column (nothing aggregates
delays by machine; verified), machineId keeps the first for the optional
relation, and machineLabel is now comma-aware so every screen and export shows
"Robo2 + Robo3". A single-Robo record (every existing one) is untouched and
displays exactly as before. The picker shows only when the delay code is
robot-specific, as before.

No schema change. Delay duration and all delay calculations are unchanged.
Verified: tsc clean, 651 unit tests (incl. roboDelayMachines), next build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SPqDFZ7o6eq1utS7hzoQsF
