From 4514e5c7f9baa4f9c8ff66c03ed32911022b721e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 06:51:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] robo(delays): remove the "+ Add" button -- enter delays
 inline

A delay the operator typed was saved only if they remembered to press "+ Add",
and they forgot. There is no "+ Add" now: each delay is a row you fill in, and it
is in the log the moment you enter it.

- The separate add form and its "+ Add" button are gone. The delay list always
  ends with one empty row; filling it in (code, machine(s), times, remark) is how
  a delay is added, and a fresh empty row appears beneath it for the next -- so
  many delays go in without a button, and none is lost to a forgotten click.
- The searchable code picker and "add a new delay code" are preserved, moved into
  a self-contained DelayCodePicker so every row carries its own. Machine
  multi-select, times, duration and remove are unchanged, per row. Empty rows are
  dropped on save.
- The reconcile save (update / create / delete), multi-Robo storage, delay
  durations, validation and all business logic are unchanged.

Removed the now-unused add-form state and handlers. UI-only change; no schema and
no API change. Verified: tsc clean, 651 unit tests, next build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SPqDFZ7o6eq1utS7hzoQsF
