From de5ebaf3a9c6a0cc78434e905dac07c50683da10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 07:20:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] robo(slabs): keep Slab Records filters through Open ->
 Edit -> Save -> return

Match the Chromia Slab Records behaviour: once the operator applies any
filter, it stays applied while they open a slab, edit it, save and come
back -- so a filtered month (say Batch No. 1423) can be worked slab after
slab without retyping the filter each time. Filters clear only on Clear
Filters, survive normal navigation, and (acceptably) survive a manual
refresh; closing the tab drops them.

Two surgical changes; the search, Edit and Save logic are untouched.

- SlabsBrowser: persist the applied filters in sessionStorage. They are
  saved on every search (a search with none clears them -- that is Clear
  Filters), and restored on mount before the list loads, so a remount
  after navigating away re-runs the same filtered search instead of the
  default latest-records load. sessionStorage, not the URL, because this
  screen already owns its filters as client state and fetches them itself;
  persisting that state changes only the persistence, not the filtering.
  Reads/writes are guarded (SSR-safe, and private-mode/quota failures just
  mean filters do not persist).

- RoboEntryForm: a page-level slab edit now returns to Slab Records
  (/robo/slabs) on save instead of the slab's own detail page, so the
  operator lands back on the filtered list ready for the next slab. The
  list restores its filters from sessionStorage on that return.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SPqDFZ7o6eq1utS7hzoQsF
