From abedb0cd25e8d009010a65134eb8b2f9f8612522 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 10:06:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] robo(slabs): show every slab of a filtered batch, not
 just the newest 200

Slabs Records capped a FILTERED search at 200 rows (ordered newest-first),
so batch 1423 -- 301 slabs -- showed only its most recent 200, while
Reports and Downloads showed all 301. Those screens run the same filter
with no cap; the list was the odd one out, and a truncated list is worse
than a slow one because it hides slabs silently -- the operator cannot tell
"200 of 301" from "that is all there is".

A filtered search now returns EVERY match (Prisma take = undefined), the
same complete set Reports and Downloads return, and the same thing Chromia's
Slab Records does: someone working a batch wants all of it in front of them.
Unfiltered browsing of the whole register stays capped at the latest 25
(that set is unbounded); an explicit ?limit= still wins, capped at 500.

The rule is extracted into slabListTake() in slabSearch.ts and pinned in
tests/roboSlabSearch.test.ts, next to the where-builder it belongs with, so
a cap can't silently creep back onto filtered results. No schema or data
change; the where-clause and every other behaviour are untouched.

