Subject: [PATCH 06/12] robo(entry): add "Close Batch" button between Edit
 setup and New batch

The Robo Entry page had no way to END a running batch: the most recent
setup stayed "running" until a New batch superseded it, so between runs
there was no "nothing is running now" state and a stray slab could still be
logged to a finished batch. Operators asked for an explicit close.

"Close Batch" sits between "Edit setup" and "New batch". Clicking it drops
the running batch to none for this session -- the page reads "No batch
running" and the slab form stops accepting entries -- then the operator
starts the next run with New batch (offered right there in the no-batch
state, since the setup form no longer auto-opens once the shift has batches).

This is a UI-state close with NO database change: the batch record and every
slab on it are left exactly as they are (batchClosed is client state, cleared
when the next batch is saved). A page refresh clears it too -- the accepted
trade-off for touching no schema. Slabs still In-Processing don't block the
close; they stay editable in Slabs Records as a closed shift already allows,
but the operator is warned first (the count is taken per-batch), because
closing mid-slab is more often a mis-tap than a choice.

No schema, API or business-logic change -- only the entry page's batch
running/closed presentation and the new button.

