From bfb7b4e25d51940932e3d5da0759bbfde5706e59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 10:28:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] robo(reports): add "Total Production Time" KPI + fix
 KPI order

Reports now shows four KPI cards in the requested order: Total Slabs
Produced, Total Production Time, Total Delays, Slabs / Hour. Only the new
card and the ordering change; the other three KPIs -- their queries, their
numbers, their formatting -- are untouched.

Total Production Time is the last completed slab's Out Time minus the first
slab's In Time, over EXACTLY the filtered slabs (the same recordWhere Total
Slabs counts), so it respects every Reports filter -- Batch, Date Wise, Date
Range -- and updates the moment a filter changes or clears, like the rest of
the summary. Batch 1428, first In 11:30, last Out 17:52 -> 6 hours 22 minutes.

It is deliberately NOT the shift open-to-close time that slabs/hour uses:
that measures when the tablet was open, this measures when the slabs
themselves started and finished. It is also date-aware -- In/Out are bare
"HH:MM", so each is paired with the slab's production date (productionDateOf:
per-slab, then setup, then shift) before the earliest In and latest Out are
taken, so a run past midnight or a multi-day filter measures a real distance,
not a min/max over clock strings. No timezone enters (the module holds every
date/time as a wall-clock string; the difference cancels the anchor), and the
wall clock is never consulted: an open run with nothing completed has no span
and the card reads "-", rather than counting up to now.

Missing/null In or Out times are skipped safely. The span logic is a pure
helper (src/lib/robo/productionSpan.ts) pinned by tests, incl. the 6h22m
example, midnight roll-over, multi-date, and every empty/negative/null case.
Shown with the same long duration format as Total Delays so the two read
alike. No schema, DB or business-logic change.

