Subject: [PATCH 08/12] =?UTF-8?q?robo(reports):=20"Avg=20Slabs/hour"=20KPI?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20Total=20Slabs=20=C3=B7=20batch=20duration,=20no?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20clock?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rename the fourth KPI from "Slabs / Hour" to "Avg Slabs/hour" and recompute
it the way it was confirmed:

  Avg Slabs/hour = Total Slabs Produced ÷ elapsed batch duration (hours)

where the duration is the production span (first In Time → last Out Time of
the filtered slabs, the Total Production Time card) with DELAYS LEFT IN, not
subtracted. 46 slabs across a 14:10 → 21:50 run (7h 40m) = 46 ÷ 7.6667 ≈ 6.0.

Why: the old figure divided Total Slabs by the SHIFT open-time, and for any
still-open shift that open-time was measured up to the current wall clock
(new Date()). So the value drifted downward as a shift stayed open even
though no slab changed -- the "changes over time with unchanged data" bug,
the same root cause as the trend chart -- and a batch filter divided the
batch's slabs by the whole shift's hours, reading far too low. The new figure
divides the SAME filtered slabs by their OWN recorded span, so it is
deterministic (identical data -> identical number, no drift) and
filter-correct (a batch's slabs over the batch's own window).

- New pure helper avgSlabsPerHour(totalSlabs, spanMinutes) in productionSpan.ts,
  pinned by tests incl. the 46-slab/7h40m example, delays-not-subtracted,
  rounding, and the null/zero/negative-span guards ("—").
- Summary route now returns avgSlabsPerHour (from the span it already computes)
  and the clock-based shift-minutes path is REMOVED entirely -- no more
  new Date()/nowMins, and two now-dead DB queries (distinct shiftId + shifts)
  are gone, so the endpoint is fully deterministic. productionMinutes and the
  old slabsPerHour are dropped from the response; nothing else consumed them
  (the trend chart, MIS sheet and telegram reports use their own fields).
- ReportsClient: card relabelled "Avg Slabs/hour", reads the new field, "—"
  when null. The other three KPIs are untouched.

No schema, DB or business-logic change.

