From d541fe7f4283e61c52a5fc4806d87410c05f6093 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 12:03:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] robo(reports): fix "Production Rate per Hour" timeline
 across midnight + date markers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause: the hourly bucketing placed each slab purely by its stored
per-slab production date. That is right ONLY when the operator re-dated the
batch's post-midnight slabs to the next day. When they didn't (a cross-
midnight run left entirely on the start date), those slabs folded back BEFORE
the batch start and the second half of the run was dropped or mis-bucketed --
"some batches completely/partially wrong". Same-day batches were fine, which
is why it looked intermittent. No wall clock was involved (that part was
already deterministic).

The timeline is now reconstructed from the production SEQUENCE as well as the
dates, so it is right either way:

- Slabs are walked in register order (serialNumber, then createdAt -- the
  route now fetches and orders by these). A completion time that jumps more
  than 12h BACKWARDS against the run so far is a midnight crossing the date
  didn't capture, so the day is advanced for it. A correct per-slab date still
  advances the day too; either signal alone places the slab correctly, and a
  small out-of-order backstep never trips a false crossing. Proven by test:
  a NOT-re-dated cross-midnight batch now yields the identical chart to the
  re-dated one, and every existing case still passes.

- Each hour bucket now carries its calendar DATE (derived from its absolute
  day, UTC, no timezone drift). The chart draws a dated marker at each midnight
  the run crossed -- 23:00-00:00 flows straight into 00:00-01:00 with no gap --
  and the card subtitle names the production date (or first -> last range).

Same-day runs still show only their real hours (11:00 … 19:00, never
00:00-24:00); the axis is still the dynamic first-In -> last-Out window; still
no wall clock, so historical hours never change. Chart UI/style unchanged --
only the data, grouping, date handling and the added date markers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SPqDFZ7o6eq1utS7hzoQsF
